 AI and AII, interpolating between the R-matrix presentation and the Drinfeld presentation. Then we formulate and provide parabolic presentations for the shifted twisted Yangians. We define quotient algebras known as truncated shifted twisted Yangians and equip them with baby comultiplications, generalizing the work of Brundan and Kl","authors":["Kang Lu","Yung-Ning Peng","Lukas Tappeiner"],"year":"2025"},"arXiv:1003.2332":{"abstract":"We begin a study of torsion theories for representations of an important class of associative algebras over a field which includes all finite W-algebras of type A, in particular the universal enveloping algebra of gl(n) (or sl(n)) for all n. If U is such and algebra which contains a finitely generated commutative subalgebra A, then we show that any A-torsion theory defined by the coheight of prime","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Serge Ovsienko","Manuel Saorin"],"year":"2010"},"arXiv:2406.05492":{"abstract":"In this paper we introduce the shifted twisted Yangian of type {\\sf AI}, following the work of Lu--Wang--Zhang, and we study their semiclassical limits, a class of Poisson algebras. We demonstrate that they coincide with the Dirac reductions of the semiclassical shifted Yangian for $\\mathfrak{gl}_n$. We deduce that these shifted twisted Yangians admit truncations which are isomorphic to Slodowy sl","authors":["Lukas Tappeiner","Lewis Topley"],"year":"2024"},"arXiv:2202.09934":{"abstract":"Let $\\mathfrak{M}_0$ be an affine Nakajima quiver variety, and $\\mathcal{M}$ is the corresponding BFN Coulomb branch. Assume that $\\mathfrak{M}_0$ can be resolved by the (smooth) Nakajima quiver variety $\\mathfrak{M}$. The Hikita-Nakajima conjecture claims that there should be an isomorphism of (graded) algebras $H^*_{S}(\\mathfrak{M},\\mathbb{C}) \\simeq \\mathbb{C}[\\mathcal{M}_{\\mathfrak{s}}^{\\mathb","authors":["Vasily Krylov","Pavel Shlykov"],"year":"2022"},"arXiv:2604.25462":{"abstract":"The evaluation homomorphism from the super Yangian $\\mathrm Y(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n})$ to the universal enveloping algebra $\\mathrm U(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n})$ allows one to regard the $\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n}$-modules as $\\mathrm Y(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n})$-modules. In this paper, we establish necessary and sufficient conditions for simple tensor products of covariant evaluation modules to be tame. We also prov","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Zheng Li","Jian Zhang"],"year":"2026"},"arXiv:1505.03619":{"abstract":"We prove how the Yangian of $\\mathfrak{gl}_N$ in its RTT presentation and Olshanski's twisted Yangians for the orthogonal and symplectic Lie algebras can be obtained by a degeneration process from the corresponding quantum loop algebra and some of its twisted analogues.","authors":["Patrick Conner","Nicolas Guay"],"year":"2015"},"arXiv:1907.03213":{"abstract":"Our purpose is to give new proofs of several known results about perturbations of matrix pencils. Andrzej Pokrzywa (1986) described the closure of orbit of a Kronecker canonical pencil $A-λB$ in terms of inequalities with pencil invariants. In more detail, Pokrzywa described all Kronecker canonical pencils $K-λL$ such that each neighborhood of $A-λB$ contains a pencil whose Kronecker canonical for","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Klymchuk","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2019"}}}